                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "19819800",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198002870741",
                            "num_reviews": 140,
                            "playtime_forever": 331,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 331,
                            "last_played": 1450601740
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "You´re appointed as new CEO of the leading firm for Hightech, Witchcraft and Extraterristic science. Now doesn´t that sound just splendid?\n\nSadly this has to be the first choose your own adventure ebooks, which really fell flat for me in some regards. \nThe development of your own character skills is at nearly no point an important decision, the only thing that matters is research and the stats of the enterprise. While this may be realistic for a CEO, it is kinda dull and mainly influenced through the budget sessions.\n\nAlso the romance part (which for this kind of game should normally offer some options) is a bit lackluster... i kind of got forced into the gay romance line, as he was the only one available.. which didnt matter much anyway in the end.\n\nRegarding the story, it also got somewhat over the top for me, when time travelling became an issue. That´s naturally a very personal taste, but that part just didn´t work out for me.\n\nTo round it up, the end game also has some bugs into it, where people appear twice, while they should be actually dead already (mind you, that was also an important part of the ending judgement, so no small lapsus imo).\n\nSo, while the writing is mostly ok the overall game just had me dissapointed, especially so, since the premise made me very interested in it.\n\nConclusio: You surely can get more refined CYoA books by now, so if you´re no hardcore fan of the topic, you can skip this one.\n\nRating: 5/10",
